usbip-win2 -- https://github.com/vadimgrn/usbip-win2

No usbip-win2 code or header is part of this project's source; its public
headers documented the USB/IP wire format that emulator/ds5emu/wire.py
implements independently. usbip-win2 is licensed under the 2-Clause BSD
License as of release 0.9.7.0 and later (earlier releases were GPL-3.0); this
project targets 0.9.7.7.

The standard installer (ds5bridge-setup-<version>.exe) and scripts/install.ps1
do not redistribute usbip-win2 or HidHide: they download each vendor's official
installer from its own release page and verify its SHA-256 before running it.

A "bundled" build of the installer (file name ending in -bundled.exe) may also
be published. It embeds, unmodified and byte-for-byte, the official installers
USBip-0.9.7.7-x64.exe (usbip-win2, BSD-2-Clause, (c) 2021-2026 Vadym
Hrynchyshyn) and HidHide_1.5.230_x64.exe (HidHide, (c) Nefarius Software
Solutions e.U.), each installed as a separate product under its own licence.
For that build the vendors' copyright and licence notices are reproduced in
app/packaging/bundle/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt, which the bundled installer
places next to the uninstaller in %LOCALAPPDATA%\ds5bridge, as the BSD-2-Clause
licence requires for binary redistribution. Neither project endorses ds5bridge.

